<section>
  <grid spacing="medium">
    <grid-item colspan="22" padding="0">
      <ai-image prompt="Ink-and-opaque-pigment editorial illustration on warm dó-paper-like fibers, an imagined non-documentary literary portrait of Nguyễn Du seated near an unlettered manuscript folio, reserved expression, Vietnamese woodblock-inspired contours, lampblack robes with muted old gold and indigo details, soft window light, no text or lettering" image-style="vietnamese-manuscript-editorial" aspect-ratio="portrait" fill="true"/>
    </grid-item>
    <grid-item colspan="38" vertical-align="center">
      <h2>Nguyễn Du and the work</h2>
      <p><b>Nguyễn Du (1765–1820)</b> created a defining work of Vietnamese literature. <i>Truyện Kiều</i>, or <i>The Tale of Kiều</i>, comprises 3,254 lines written in chữ Nôm and composed in lục bát verse.</p>
      <p>Its achievement is both narrative and formal: a long story sustained through voice, rhyme, cadence, and ethical tension.</p>
      <grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug">
        <grid-item colspan="20" vertical-align="center">
          <display font-size="30pt">1765–1820</display>
          <h4>Nguyễn Du</h4>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="20" vertical-align="center">
          <display font-size="40pt">3,254</display>
          <h4>Lines</h4>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="20" vertical-align="center">
          <display font-size="32pt">lục bát</display>
          <h4>Form</h4>
          <p font-size="sm">Composed in chữ Nôm.</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
      <p font-size="sm">Interpretive illustration. Sources: <a href="https://baotangvanhoc.vn/hien-vat-hinh-anh/hien-vat-len-tieng/truyen-kieu-mot-kiet-tac-van-hoc/">Vietnamese Literature Museum</a>; <a href="https://www.nomfoundation.org/nom-project/Tale-of-Kieu?uiLang=vn">Vietnamese Nôm Preservation Foundation</a>.</p>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>